vtcity for Atari System V and AMIX
==================================

vtcity is tenox7's port of Micropolis (the open-source SimCity) to DEC
VT320/340/420 terminals with downloadable fonts
(github.com/tenox7/vtcity), built as a static AMIX program.  On Atari
System V it runs through the service pack's amx module
(github.com/slaapliedje/atari-sysv-sp1).

    vtcity                 asks the terminal what it is
    vtcity -noquery -t 420 skip the question and draw for a VT420

It needs a terminal or emulator that takes DEC soft fonts (DECDLD): a real
VT320 or later, or an emulator that implements them.  A plain xterm shows letters in place
of the tiles.  For those, use ttycity.

Installed under /opt/vtcity (bin, lib, share/cities, doc), with
/usr/bin/vtcity linking to the command.

Install as root:   pkgadd -d vtcity-VERSION.pkg VTCITY
Remove:            pkgrm VTCITY

Source: github.com/slaapliedje/asv-games has the build scripts and the
exact upstream commit (no source changes).  Licence: GPL-3.0 with the
Micropolis additional terms (LICENSE here).
